intro:
Marathi has three main ways to talk about the future:

• the **-णार** form for plans and things that are going to happen: मी जाणार आहे 'I'm going to go' (Unit 13);
• the **simple future** for promises, predictions and offers: मी फोन करेन 'I'll call', पाऊस पडेल 'it will rain';
• **dative + -आयचं आहे** for what you want or intend to do: मला गोव्याला जायचं आहे 'I want to go to Goa'.

In everyday speech the -णार form is the most common of all.
